<title>USA: USDA sets 1997 marketing assistance loan rates.</title>
<headline>USDA sets 1997 marketing assistance loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Friday said it set marketing assistance loan rates for 1997 crop wheat, feed grains and oilseeds at the maximum levels allowed by law.</p>
<p>USDA said the marketing assistance loan rates for 1997 crops were as follows:</p>
<p>    Wheat:	    $2.58 per bushel</p>
<p>    Corn:	     $1.89 per bushel</p>
<p>    Soybeans:	 $5.26 per bushel</p>
<p>    Sorghum:	  $1.76 per bushel</p>
<p>Minor Oilseeds: $9.30 per hundredweight</p>
<p>    Barley:	   $1.57 per bushel</p>
<p>    Oats:	     $1.11 per bushel</p>
<p>USDA said producers have placed 182 million bushels of wheat, 952 million bushels of feed grains and 188 million bushels of soybeans under loan through January 28. That compares with 114 million bushels of wheat, 676 million bushels of corn and 182 million bushels of soybeans for the entire 1995 crop.</p>
